      "writtenOn": "2015-01-05T23:16:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "And this one: `keystone.assignment.role.core.Driver`\n\n---\n\nIn few words, the rationally is: keystone.assignment.engine is something that uses everything in keystone.assignment (except for \u0027role\u0027 and itself) and returns what an actor can do on a resource, i.e, keystone.assignment.role.\n\n---\n\nLike this, it would be easier to the deployer to add a new assignment logic. She only needs to completly drop `keystone.assignment.engine` and plug her own implementation.\nAs we have today, she would need to delete the engine Driver class (that hasn\u0027t an appropriate name and is inside the same file of RoleDriver) and provide her implementation.\n\nNote that `keystone.assignment.role` will never be removed, since it handles what really matters: the roles/capabilities, that goes in the token.\n\nIn addition, it would be easier to:\n\ni) add a new `keystone.assignment.domain_role`, if needed;\n\nii) rename `keystone.assignment.role` to `keystone.assignment.capability` and `keystone.assignment.domain_role` to `keystone.assignment.role`, if needed;\n\niii) add a new `keystone.assignment.\u003cattribute_X\u003e`, if needed.",
      "revId": "9dfc5702b31d2fff6c0b79c23fe11f551fa90428",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
